From a8ff3103049317564fa72f287a0392971498e10f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yusuke Hayashi <yusuke8h@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:05:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hayro-syntax: Let callers budget and cancel object parsing

Add `budget::ParseBudget`, which a caller passes to
`FromBytes::from_bytes_with_budget`. The reader charges the bytes it
advances over in windows of 4 KiB, so the budget can poll a deadline or a
cancellation during one large object, and the parser charges the buffers
of escaped names and strings and the entry table of dictionaries before
allocating them, releasing the table when the dictionary is dropped. Lazy
reads of dictionary entries and array items charge the same budget.

A refusal moves the reader to the end of its data, so every loop ends.
`from_bytes_with_budget` returns `Exhausted` after a refusal rather than an
object that the parser recovered from the cut data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
